Chapter: Clipboard
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 Clipboard abstraction -- read/write for text and binary data.
 The clipboard is modeled as a pure data store; actual system
 integration happens at the platform boundary (UEFI, OS, or
 hosted environment).

 To clipboard-empty gives an empty clipboard.
 To clipboard-set-text gives a clipboard with text content.
 To clipboard-get-text gives the text content if present.
 To clipboard-set-bytes gives a clipboard with binary content.
 To clipboard-get-bytes gives the binary content if present.
 To clipboard-clear gives an emptied clipboard.

 We say:

Section: Types

  ClipboardContent =
    | ClipEmpty
    | ClipText (Text)
    | ClipBytes (List Integer) (Text)

  Clipboard = record {
    cb-content : ClipboardContent,
    cb-sequence : Integer
  }

Section: Construction

  clipboard-empty : Clipboard = Clipboard {
    cb-content = ClipEmpty,
    cb-sequence = 0
  }

  clipboard-set-text : Clipboard, Text -> Clipboard
  clipboard-set-text (cb) (text) = Clipboard {
    cb-content = ClipText text,
    cb-sequence = cb.cb-sequence + 1
  }

  clipboard-set-bytes : Clipboard, List Integer, Text -> Clipboard
  clipboard-set-bytes (cb) (data) (mime) = Clipboard {
    cb-content = ClipBytes data mime,
    cb-sequence = cb.cb-sequence + 1
  }

  clipboard-clear : Clipboard -> Clipboard
  clipboard-clear (cb) = Clipboard {
    cb-content = ClipEmpty,
    cb-sequence = cb.cb-sequence + 1
  }

Section: Queries

  clipboard-get-text : Clipboard -> Maybe Text
  clipboard-get-text (cb) = when cb.cb-content
    is ClipText (t) -> Just t
    is otherwise -> None

  clipboard-get-bytes : Clipboard -> Maybe (List Integer)
  clipboard-get-bytes (cb) = when cb.cb-content
    is ClipBytes (data) (mime) -> Just data
    is otherwise -> None

  clipboard-has-text : Clipboard -> Boolean
  clipboard-has-text (cb) = when cb.cb-content
    is ClipText (t) -> True
    is otherwise -> False

  clipboard-has-bytes : Clipboard -> Boolean
  clipboard-has-bytes (cb) = when cb.cb-content
    is ClipBytes (data) (mime) -> True
    is otherwise -> False

  clipboard-is-empty : Clipboard -> Boolean
  clipboard-is-empty (cb) = when cb.cb-content
    is ClipEmpty -> True
    is otherwise -> False

  clipboard-mime-type : Clipboard -> Text
  clipboard-mime-type (cb) = when cb.cb-content
    is ClipText (t) -> "text/plain"
    is ClipBytes (data) (mime) -> mime
    is ClipEmpty -> ""

  clipboard-sequence : Clipboard -> Integer
  clipboard-sequence (cb) = cb.cb-sequence

